      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "See equivalent in the Servlet stack"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "web/webmvc/mvc-controller/ann-initbinder.html#mvc-ann-initbinder-model-design"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "span",
                "roles": [
                  "small"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Data binding"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "core/validation/beans-beans.html#beans-binding"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for web requests involves binding request parameters to a model object. By default, request parameters can be bound to any public property of the model object, which means malicious clients can provide extra values for properties that exist in the model object graph, but are not expected to be set. This is why model object design requires careful consideration."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The model object, and its nested object graph is also sometimes referred to as a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "command object"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "form-backing object"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "POJO"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (Plain Old Java Object)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A good practice is to use a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "dedicated model object"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " rather than exposing your domain model such as JPA or Hibernate entities for web data binding. For example, on a form to change an email address, create a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ChangeEmailForm"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " model object that declares only the properties required for the input:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "public class ChangeEmailForm {\n\n\tprivate String oldEmailAddress;\n\tprivate String newEmailAddress;\n\n\tpublic void setOldEmailAddress(String oldEmailAddress) {\n\t\tthis.oldEmailAddress = oldEmailAddress;\n\t}\n\n\tpublic String getOldEmailAddress() {\n\t\treturn this.oldEmailAddress;\n\t}\n\n\tpublic void setNewEmailAddress(String newEmailAddress) {\n\t\tthis.newEmailAddress = newEmailAddress;\n\t}\n\n\tpublic String getNewEmailAddress() {\n\t\treturn this.newEmailAddress;\n\t}\n\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Another good practice is to apply "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "constructor binding"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "core/validation/beans-beans.html#beans-constructor-binding"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", which uses only the request parameters it needs for constructor arguments, and any other input is ignored. This is in contrast to property binding which by default binds every request parameter for which there is a matching property."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If neither a dedicated model object nor constructor binding is sufficient, and you must use property binding, we strongly recommend registering "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "allowedFields"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " patterns (case sensitive) on "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebDataBinder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in order to prevent unexpected properties from being set. For example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Controller\npublic class ChangeEmailController {\n\n\t@InitBinder\n\tvoid initBinder(WebDataBinder binder) {\n\t\tbinder.setAllowedFields(\"oldEmailAddress\", \"newEmailAddress\");\n\t}\n\n\t// @RequestMapping methods, etc.\n\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can also register "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "disallowedFields"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " patterns (case insensitive). However, \"allowed\" configuration is preferred over \"disallowed\" as it is more explicit and less prone to mistakes."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, constructor and property binding are both used. If you want to use constructor binding only, you can set the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "declarativeBinding"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " flag on "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebDataBinder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " through an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@InitBinder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method either locally within a controller or globally through an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@ControllerAdvice"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Turning this flag on ensures that only constructor binding is used and that property binding is not used unless "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "allowedFields"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " patterns are configured. For example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Controller\npublic class MyController {\n\n\t@InitBinder\n\tvoid initBinder(WebDataBinder binder) {\n\t\tbinder.setDeclarativeBinding(true);\n\t}\n\n\t// @RequestMapping methods, etc.\n\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
